  "system": {
    "identifier": "shikigami-origami-technique-paper-shuriken",
    "description": "<p>You create razor-sharp origami shuriken, and launch them at your foe. Make a ranged ninjutsu attack dealing 4d4 slashing damage.</p>\n<p>Paper Veil. If this jutsu is cast while your Paper Veil state is active, it gains the benefit of your first Canvas Type.</p>\n<p>Explosive Veil. On a hit, the shuriken detonate, forcing the target creature, and all creatures within 10 feet of the target to make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d6 fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success.</p>\n<p>Serrated Veil. On a hit, the affected creature makes a Constitution saving throw, gaining a rank of Bleed on a failure.</p>\n<p>Binding Veil. On a hit, the affected creature makes a Charisma saving throw, gaining a rank of Sealed on a failure.</p>\n<p>Weaving Veil. On a hit, you move up to your speed, and if you end your movement within range of a target, you can make one unarmed attack against them.</p>\n<p>Origami Angel/Demon. If this jutsu is cast while in your Origami Angel/Demon state this jutsu’s range becomes Self (30-foot cone), comparing your attack result, vs the AC of all creatures in range.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost by 3, the attacks damage by 2d4 and all other damage by +1 damage die. If this jutsu is cast at B-Rank or higher, increase the ranks of conditions inflicted and unarmed attacks made by +1. If this jutsu is cast at S-Rank, increase the ranks of conditions inflicted and unarmed attacks made by +1.</p>",
    "source": {
